  "result": "I looked through the app first. The site builds the timetable page from `sailings.csv`, which the ferry office exports each night. Nothing in that file marks a sailing as cancelled, and there's no code for warnings yet. So the site currently has no way of knowing that a sailing is off.\n\nThat makes the biggest open question where the news of a cancellation would come from. Whether this is a new column in the nightly file, a way for staff to flag a sailing during the day, or something else depends on how cancellations actually happen. It also decides how quickly a warning could reach people, since a nightly export can't cover a sailing that's called off at noon because of weather.\n\nWhen a sailing gets cancelled today, how does that decision get made, and how do passengers currently find out about it?",
